From: CosmosEx Buildroot <4372835+planeturban@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:55:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ce_main_app: Files page API (/api/v1/files), two panes as
 Midnight Commander

GET places, list, read (download), zip (several files and folders, made as
it's sent); POST write (the body as a file, streamed to the tool's stdin),
mkdir, delete, rename. A place is /storage, a translated drive folder, a
USB drive, the shared drive or a partition of a hard disk image. The work
is done by the image's /usr/sbin/ce-files (run without a shell; paths kept
inside the place, no links followed); a download's headers are sent only
once the tool's output isn't an error report.

Attaching a hard disk image first closes its session on the Files page
(ce-hdinspect close; refused while a file in it is in use): the ST mustn't
share an image with a mount.
